  "id": "nonlinear-relationship",
  "term": "nonlinear relationship",
  "definition": "A nonlinear relationship is a link between two variables in which changes in one are not matched by a simple straight-line increase or decrease in the other. In psychology research, this means the association can vary across different levels of the variable rather than staying constant.",
